    {
      "id": "e6902faca2d7834484ba3d8ee4a86df6c04a82f0",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1212448947,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I think why you were seeing an extra stream number is that below creates a new conversation with even if the UDP conversation existed but didn't have its handle set to SNMP. The behavior would have worked without allocating a new stream number creating a conversation only when it couldn't find one (and then setting the conversation dissector to either the existing conversation or the newly created one.)\n\nHowever, I think long term, we probably do want to create conversations of many different types, just remember that the dissector usually needs to be set to the port type conversation, since that's what the lower level (UDP, TCP, etc.) dissector checks to send dissection here in the first place.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
