        {
          "id": 1212770857,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I'll need to draw a picture. :-)  \nWhat happens with a UDP conversation that isn't all SNMP packets?  \n  \nI was chasing this - [Duplicated UDP stream IDs?](https://ask.wireshark.org/question/29948/duplicated-udp-stream-ids/) - and saw that the UDP total at the top of the Conversations did not match that last stream ID in the column. That was with the \"original Ultimate pcap\" that also has an issue with UDP streams inside ICMP error messages.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-12-16T15:18:44.282Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-12-16T15:20:55.487Z",
