        {
          "id": 2349209884,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I'm currently working on !19034 which is bringing back `CONVERSATION_SNMP`. The idea of this new MR is to handle the SNMP conversation and to do some work for the underlying UDP conversation (by associating the SNMP dissector). Unpredictable ephemeral server ports are a problem because the way we are identifying conversations is _greedy_ (try that, and that, and that and that..) which at the end will match something we don't want. For this reason I'm suggesting a non-greedy option (try to find the matching conversation, in all cases return immediately without trying do that and that and that). I'll update the MR when the previous one is merged.",
